 form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106842/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a4d10f94-98d4-53d8-a35c-e65a06dd2c55"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106842"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75093/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "f739fae0-7682-5b46-9c7e-7cebd203bed1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75093/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "86246cee-28ab-5eb6-84bf-b2ee1b0b7456" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75093/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "b4440c05-eb53-5ba4-a6b9-3ef96029cea0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75093/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "4314a9a2-18d6-5135-b52f-f669d5e8ca45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75093/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "d5bb3222-a3a8-534c-8d18-8262eb5ef6f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75093/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6df1d8e-1523-5a0c-b598-780e058adb9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75093/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer-field/choices ["q-75093/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-75093/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-75093/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-75093/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-75093/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75093" :question/id #uuid "5389cdd5-577a-5ad9-b29c-11a69f6cb769" :question/math-academy-id "q-75093" :question/problem "Given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{33}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{32}=-\\frac{1}{2},{u}_{33}=3,$ and ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{33}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75093/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a4d10f94-98d4-53d8-a35c-e65a06dd2c55"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75093"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32581/selection/b2780c45573e209dad3ebc748a022789392cf9603b4f858d2ba97362c5db3873" :answer/id #uuid "cde6e73f-ce5f-5272-9481-328a2c32b77d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32581/selection/fa3f81dbe0334d852765b790b974fcac4427c0d8ba6f022dab43ba96906f851c" :answer/id #uuid "1051df50-4e74-5a89-a604-f62d80a08bd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32581/selection/13851ec9dcff6d611c6c9ba58e73dcc0bd84173f62e01dde4de2656c21a64c35" :answer/id #uuid "6ce7cb90-e79a-59dc-8c2c-802481fc934e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id