}_{1} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-32581/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a4d10f94-98d4-53d8-a35c-e65a06dd2c55"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32581"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32685/selection/d414241716b05822a299bbf6605e609e3b3741b210c0adca6db9f925b8cb6a0c" :answer/id #uuid "4bfc9c8c-a567-5caf-ac86-6c880db1c4d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32685/selection/497b2c9c9fd1dfc81fb8d0fe7daa316f5c2edd51e7da460c0a25df14a4d9bd73" :answer/id #uuid "13597c39-7c68-51a7-8766-3e059d7fe2f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32685/selection/4638fe97cd71c18af746bd2275a0435e3182783b1c1d655a789a99878ed2474e" :answer/id #uuid "b1626c63-8aaa-5bbb-8f30-c6dfcdb97792" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32685/selection/8c659233096a066737dda9d148b3542eb7a6f